{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqft8cz9ula","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"OVERRIDE: merged hookless-worker gate fix is LIVE but still denies background worker writes — root cause is claim session vs harness session mismatch","summary":"SPEC IS INCOMPLETE: the prior note claiming the gate fix is \"done-but-unmerged\" is now stale. Verified 2026-06-15 against live code + running daemon: commit 137bbf3 (the agent_tool_spawn match leg in /active-claim) IS merged on main AND loaded in the live daemon (PID 56853, booted 16:25 EDT, after the 14:29 file write of routes/session.js). A restart does NOT help. A run_in_background Agent-tool worker that did branch_task + start_task ok was STILL denied at the orch-gate.\n\nPrecise root cause: orch-gate.sh:43 queries /active-claim?session=$SID where SID = the hook input .session_id (the WRITING worker's harness session). /active-claim (routes/session.js:24-44) has three match legs: (1) subagent_session===sid — nulled by touchAgent for self-registered workers; (2) agent_tool_spawn && session===sid — agent_tool_spawn is never set because SubagentStart does not fire for run_in_background spawns; (3) claimSessions[task_key]===sid. Leg 3 is the only viable one, BUT claimSessions is populated ONLY by an explicit POST /overlay/claim-session (routes/overlay.js:356-363) with whatever session_id that caller passes — it is NOT set by start_task, and the recorded session_id does not equal the worker's harness .session_id the gate reads. So all three legs miss, /session-info returns is_subagent:false, the gate treats the worker as an unclaimed MAIN session and denies (main-session deny message).\n\nFix direction (NOT yet applied; needs gate-off to edit gated orchestrator source): make the worker's harness session_id flow into claimSessions at start_task time (so leg 3 matches), OR add an /active-claim leg that honors a registered-worktree-backed claim by agent_id independent of session (weigh against the worktree-as-security-boundary invariant). Until then, background-subagent dispatch for file-writing work is non-functional; the working unblock is 'orch off' + inline edits (or ORCH_GATE_OFF=1 spawn-env for scripted harness workers, which is how the learner-drain script gets throu","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-15T22:54:02.421Z","vec":[-0.10027524083852768,0.02053055353462696,-0.021974528208374977,0.015329569578170776,0.03468504175543785,-0.04577271640300751,0.027253687381744385,0.014543537050485611,-0.00233188783749938,0.07824545353651047,-0.005693555809557438,-0.019413575530052185,0.011618309654295444,-0.007590462453663349,0.017193961888551712,0.02830333448946476,0.027971133589744568,-0.005656891502439976,-0.04073108360171318,-0.05713936313986778,0.048619769513607025,0.04333148151636124,0.008721370249986649,0.04561707377433777,-0.031976912170648575,-0.0784507766366005,-0.05968181788921356,-0.016663284972310066,-0.01974203623831272,-0.02767244726419449,-0.04436901584267616,0.07969966530799866,-0.1192345842719078,-0.07534682005643845,0.058759503066539764,0.08570535480976105,0.014971002005040646,-0.002536853775382042,-0.028490539640188217,0.00040779158007353544,0.057959966361522675,0.03560444712638855,-0.05937432497739792,-0.10182404518127441,-0.06466817855834961,-0.01816227100789547,-0.043964482843875885,-0.02803952805697918,-0.0400567352771759,0.000786944932769984,0.020823275670409203,-0.00771627202630043,0.08548564463853836,0.06139510124921799,-0.003456707112491131,0.015398259274661541,0.012946760281920433,0.04183834791183472,-0.024096254259347916,0.046669211238622665,0.003537008073180914,0.013427565805613995,0.0021754419431090355,-0.031276635825634,0.004003266338258982,0.05777539312839508,0.007571009453386068,-0.06759008765220642,0.02951246127486229,-0.034732937812805176,0.021825507283210754,-0.03088359162211418,-0.08527083694934845,-0.07127267122268677,0.0246528722345829,0.0068095591850578785,0.007877010852098465,0.022228676825761795,0.0028867998626083136,-0.19286105